  "question": "Can the pin run copy's own PDFs stand in for the 7 missing pdf-probe pairs, and is the re-render equivalent?",
  "step1": {
    "commands": "node <scratch>/step1.mjs (pdfWordsV2 + chromeWordsFingerprint from fidelity/layout-diff/lib over the pin run copy's corpus/ and oracles/ chrome.pdf; sha256 of corpus templated.html and layout-diff native.html/browser.html in the pin, 00-start and 09 run copies)",
    "reading": "The pin run copy has no layout-diff PDFs for these 7 (its pdf-probe ran --fixtures notification,invoice). Its corpus/oracle Chrome PDFs have the chain's Chrome word fingerprint (all but oracles/corpus/oss-postmark-receipt/plain/reference/chrome.pdf), and corpus templated.html = layout-diff native.html (same sha256) in all three runs; but its corpus/oracle vellora.pdf are NOT the pdf-probe producer's bytes (oracles/fixtures/invoice/plain/vellora.pdf 8f915a8f... != layout-diff 5c406133..., same PyMuPDF words). So the vellora side was re-rendered with the pdf-probe producer at the pin (inputMap in manifest.pdfProbeRescore), and the pin run copy's PDFs serve as a cross-check.",
    "date": "2026-10-22T22:24:51.313Z",
